{% comment %}
  RAQI — floating WhatsApp button (mobile).

  The header's WhatsApp icon carries .rd-hide-sm, which raqi-redesign.css hides
  at max-width 900px. This is its mobile counterpart, so the two are mirror
  images of one breakpoint: the float appears at exactly 900px and below, the
  header icon at 901px and above. Change one and you must change the other or
  there will be a width with two buttons or none.

  Number is also in sections/rd-header.liquid, sections/footer-group.json and
  templates/page.contact.json — keep the four in sync.

  Placement uses inset-inline-end, so it sits bottom-right under LTR and
  bottom-left under RTL with no separate rule.

  Stacking, measured against what else is fixed to the bottom of the viewport:
    .raqi-sticky-atc (product page, <=900px)  z-index 30
    .rd-sticky                                z-index 40
    THIS BUTTON                               z-index 500
    .rd-cd (cart drawer)                      z-index 900
  So the button clears both bottom bars but the cart drawer still covers it,
  which is what you want when the drawer is open.

  On product pages the sticky Add-to-Cart bar occupies the bottom of the
  viewport. It measures 59px tall at every mobile width, so the button is
  lifted clear of it there rather than sitting on top of it.
{% endcomment %}
<a
  class="raqi-wa-float"
  href="https://wa.me/971585670055"
  target="_blank"
  rel="noopener"
  aria-label="Chat with RAQI on WhatsApp"
